@startuml
title F11 - Caregiver dashboard and timeline
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Primary caregiver" as Caregiver
boundary "A05\nApp platform" as A05
control "B01\nIdentity/access" as B01
control "B07\nRead models/API" as B07
control "B08\nOperations/data" as B08
boundary "A02\nApp home" as A02
Caregiver -> A05: Open home dashboard
A05 -> B01: Attach verified OIDC token and require home membership
A05 -> B07: GET snapshot and ordered timeline
B07 -> B08: Read independent hub lease, diagnostics and audit-safe status
B07 --> A05: Return versioned evidence, incidents and fetched time
A05 -> A05: Accept only newer cache version; classify auth/service/network failure
A05 -> A02: Build separate activity and connectivity cards
A02 -> Caregiver: Render original time, freshness, coverage and unresolved incidents
note over A02,Caregiver: Fresh phone data cannot make stale hub data current; no activity is not a wellbeing verdict.
note over Caregiver,A02: Outcome - The caregiver sees evidence, hub reachability and incident state as separate, freshness-qualified facts.
@enduml
